 Debugging log

Status labels: Fixed, Diagnosed (cause found, fix not yet confirmed), Open.

 A. Intro loader and background video (earlier sessions)

| Problem | What was investigated |
| --- | --- |
| Loader not centered | Parent positioning, flexbox alignment, div placement |
| Progress bar positioning | Width, height, padding, parent alignment |
| Loader behaviour | Percentage logic, interval timing, CSS animation |
| Loader disappearing wrongly | The .hide class and the upward translateY(-100%) |
| Website appearing too early | Timing between loader exit and website visibility |
| Video playing under the loader | Start playback only after the loader exits (video.currentTime = 0; video.play() inside a setTimeout) |
| Video and content overlapping | Layering with position and z-index |
| Title letters appearing all at once | One <span> per letter plus animation-delay per letter |

 B. Scroll position and restoration (earlier sessions)

The page sometimes opened already scrolled into the second section after a refresh. It was investigated with window.scrollY (how far the page is scrolled) and getBoundingClientRect().top (an element's distance from the top of the viewport). Browsers restore the previous scroll position on reload by default, and history.scrollRestoration = "manual" turns that off.

 C. Reveal animations

C1. Hero reveal played before anyone could see it (Fixed)
- Symptom: the Hero letters had already finished animating by the time the section scrolled into view.
- Cause: the reveal-content class was added inside the loader's setTimeout, while the section was still below the screen. An animation starts the moment its selector matches, so the line that adds the class decides when the user sees it.
- Fix: moved classList.add("reveal-content") into the IntersectionObserver callback.

C2. Hero letters flashed instead of rising (Fixed, one cosmetic item open)
- Cause: the base style had no opacity: 0, so letters were visible during their animation-delay, vanished at the 0% keyframe, then faded back in. There was also no display: inline-block, and transform is ignored on inline elements, so the letters never moved.
- Fix: added both. The base style must match the 0% keyframe.
- Still open: the stagger delays (0.12, 0.24, 0.48, 0.6) are uneven. The title uses an even 0.12s step.

 D. Endless image strips

D1. <marquee> tag (Fixed)
- Cause: <marquee> is obsolete, speed is not one of its attributes, it leaves empty gaps, and flex was set on the wrong parent.
- Fix: replaced it with a window (.second-strip-image, overflow: hidden) and a track (.track, display: flex; width: max-content) animated with @keyframes and translateX.

D2. Gap and snap at the end of each lap (Fixed for strip 1)
- Cause: the track is two identical halves and the animation slides exactly one half. The loop only looks endless if the first and last frames are identical, and each half must be at least as wide as the viewport. If a half is narrower, the end of the track becomes visible, then the lap restarts and snaps.
- Fix: duplicate the images in JavaScript, and give matching images in both halves the same delay.

js
track.innerHTML += track.innerHTML;

track.querySelectorAll("span").forEach((span, index) => {
  span.style.transitionDelay = (index % 16) * 0.2 + "s"; // 16 = images per half
});


D3. Two animations fighting over transform (Prevented)
- Cause: .track already animates transform for the slide, so a second transform animation on the same element overrides it.
- Fix: reveal the wrapper and the individual <span>s, never .track itself.

D4. Track not displaying after the marquee swap (Cause not recorded)
- A checklist was built instead: does the selector match the HTML class name, is the rule actually being read (an unclosed } or broken comment swallows the next rule), and is the result clipped, covered or zero-sized? See [Debugging method](debugging-method).

D5. Strip 2 restarts halfway and is not smooth (Open, diagnosed)
- Direction: from: translateX(50%); to: translateX(0) makes the first and last frames different pictures, so every lap snaps back. Right to left needs from: 0; to: translateX(-50%).
- Width: strip 2 has 10 images at about 106px each (100px image plus 3px padding on each side), so one half is about 1060px, likely narrower than the window. It needs more images per half.
- No start state: .second-2ndstrip-image span has no opacity: 0 or translateY, so the per-image transition-delay has nothing to animate and the images cannot appear one by one.

 E. Visibility, thresholds and layering

E1. First strip disappeared when there were many images (Fixed, fragile)
- Symptom: the strip stayed invisible and the shows class never appeared. With fewer images it worked.
- Cause: the most an IntersectionObserver ratio can ever reach is window height divided by section height. Measured in the console: window.innerHeight was 671 and the section's offsetHeight was 3544, so the ceiling was 671 / 3544 = about 0.19. The thresholds were 0.4 and 1, which could never be reached, so the callbacks never ran and the spans stayed at opacity: 0.
- Fix: thresholds lowered to 0.1 and 0.18.
- Lessons: 0.18 is very close to the 0.19 ceiling, so on a shorter window it would fail again. Early measurements (a 1992px window) came from browser zoom at roughly 33%, so always measure at 100% zoom.
- Better long-term fix: make every section exactly 100vh and observe the specific element to reveal, so ordinary thresholds work.

E2. Second strip invisible (Fixed)
- Cause: the background video is position: absolute, and positioned elements paint on a higher layer than normal-flow ones. Strip 2 was static, so the video covered it. The images were there all along.
- Fix: position: relative (currently on the strip's images). Without offsets it does not move the element, it only changes its paint layer.
- Learned: position does two jobs: where an element is placed, and which layer it paints on. z-index only works on positioned elements.

E3. Third section measured 0 x 0 (Diagnosed)
- Cause suspected: the .third-part rule was not being applied (a broken /* ... */ comment merges text into the next selector and drops the rule, or the class name did not match). A box of 0 x 0 cannot come from width: 100%; height: 100vh.
- Learned: an absolute element with no top/left/right/bottom stays at its static position and does not jump to an ancestor. Full-screen sections should be in the flow with position: relative, as anchors for their video.
- Status: the CSS now looks valid, but the display has not been confirmed.

E4. display: flexbox (Fixed)
- Not a valid value. The correct one is display: flex.

E5. Reusing .strip-animation for strip 2 (Fixed)
- Cause: querySelector returns only the first match, so the JS line only reached strip 1. In CSS, .a.b with no space means "an element with both classes", so the rule only matched strip 1's wrapper.
- Fix: a separate strip-animation2 class with its own CSS and JS, for the second wrapper.

